<%- include('partials/page-header', { eyebrow: 'Information', heading: 'Privacy', ghost: 'privacy' }) %>
<article class="legal-content" data-reveal>
<h2>Account and session data</h2>
<p>We store your username, email address, password hash, role, and account dates. Essential session cookies keep you signed in and protect forms. Passwords are never stored in plaintext.</p>
<h2>Links and usage</h2>
<p>We store links you create, their destinations, restrictions, and click totals. Click records include the time, a keyed hash of the network address, a limited browser identifier, and the referring origin when available. We do not store raw network addresses in click analytics. Development server logs are separate from analytics.</p>
<h2>Uploads and submissions</h2>
<p>Uploaded files, ownership, file metadata, and optional expiry dates are stored. Submissions and administrator review notes are retained with your account. Uploaded files are accessible only to authorized CMS users.</p>
<h2>Retention</h2>
<p>When the scheduled cleanup command runs, it removes detailed analytics older than <%= retention %> days and expired uploads. Aggregate link click counts remain. Deleted short links stop working and retain their reserved alias and history; deleting a link does not reassign its address. Sessions expire automatically.</p>
<h2>Cookies and third parties</h2>
<p>Platform and CMS authentication use separate session cookies. There are no advertising trackers or external fonts. QR codes are generated locally. Following a shortened link takes you to the destination website, which has its own privacy policy.</p>
<h2>Account requests</h2>
<p>Contact the operator who provided your account or this installation for access, correction, or deletion requests.</p>
</article>
